// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row break_through_closure_admitted (tier 2, `admits`). Rust-parity audit 2026-09-26 (high): break / break 'label inside a closure is accepted and silently does nothing
// FLS: fls_ep5smja1rxdv fls_7hc8yboeaho0
// Logos: Compiles and links; running returns exit code 5 (the loop ran to completion, all 5 iterations) — the `break 'outer` written and executed inside the closure body has NO EFFECT on the outer loop: it is silently accepted syntacticall
// rustc: rustc 1.98.1 rejects with error[E0767]: use of unreachable label `'outer` ('labels are unreachable through functions, closures, async blocks and modules') plus error[E0267]: `break` inside of a closure.
// fix hint: sema: reset the loop/label context at closure and item boundaries (E0267 / E0767).
package break_through_closure_admitted;
fn main() -> i32 {
    let mut count: i32 = 0;
    'outer: for i in 0..5 {
        let f = || {
            break 'outer;
        };
        f();
        count = count + 1;
    }
    return count;
}
